      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "042ed918-7938-48d7-a80c-61a48b09c1fd"
        },
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail",
          "scroll": "page"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;background:#f8fbfd;font-family:Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;min-height:100%;padding:4.4cqw 7cqw 5cqw'><div style='font:700 1.3cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#be185d'>Study guide</div><div style='font:700 5.4cqw/1.1 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;margin:1.4cqw 0 .8cqw;color:#1f2937'>Graph-Based Interfaces</div><div style='font:400 2.1cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:1.6cqw;max-width:62cqw'>Explore how graphs can become the foundation of interactive software rather than merely diagrams inside applications. The goal is to understand graph structure, visual organization, navigation, semantic meaning, reusable interfaces, persistence, and AI collaboration well enough to evaluate and design a graph-native application.</div><div style='margin-top:2.6cqw;max-width:62cqw'><div style='display:flex;height:1.6cqw;border-radius:9cqw;overflow:hidden;background:#e2e8f0'><div style='flex:9 0 0;background:#cbd5e1'></div></div><div style='margin-top:1cqw;font:600 1.5cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;color:#64748b'><span style='color:#15803d'>0 solid</span> · <span style='color:#b45309'>0 shaky</span> · 9 not yet · 9 concepts</div></div><div style='margin-top:2.2cqw;font:700 2cqw/1.4 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#0369a1'>Start with Nodes, edges, and properties</div><div style='font:700 1.3cqw/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0369a1;margin:4cqw 0 1.6cqw;padding-top:2cqw;border-top:.15cqw solid rgba(3,105,161,.35)'>In the order to learn them</div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#0369a1'>1</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:.3cqw solid #0369a1'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Nodes, edges, and properties<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span><span style='margin-left:1.4cqw;color:#0369a1;font:800 1.2cqw/1 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase'>start here</span></div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>A graph consists of entities represented by nodes and relationships represented by edges. Nodes and edges can carry properties that define their meaning, appearance, and behavior. This simple structure can represent surprisingly complex information.</div><div style='margin-top:.8cqw;font:400 1.6cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155'><span style='color:#4d7c0f;font:800 1.2cqw/1 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase'>other</span> <b style='font-weight:700;color:#1f2937'>Interactive graph theory primer</b> · Look for introductory graph theory material with interactive examples.</div></div></div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#94a3b8'>2</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Graphs versus hierarchies<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span></div><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-top:.4cqw'>needs Nodes, edges, and properties</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>Traditional interfaces commonly organize information into trees: folders, menus, and nested documents. Graphs permit multiple relationships between the same entities and allow information to participate in several contexts without duplicating it.</div></div></div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#94a3b8'>3</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Graph layout and spatial organization<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span></div><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-top:.4cqw'>needs Nodes, edges, and properties</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>A graph&#39;s logical structure does not prescribe its visual arrangement. Layout algorithms position nodes and route connections to reveal relationships. Spatial organization affects readability, navigation, and the user&#39;s ability to understand complex structures.</div><div style='margin-top:.8cqw;font:400 1.6cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155'><span style='color:#4d7c0f;font:800 1.2cqw/1 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase'>article</span> <b style='font-weight:700;color:#1f2937'>Graph visualization and interaction research</b> · Search visualization research literature for graph drawing, information visualization, and semantic zoom.</div></div></div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#94a3b8'>4</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Navigation and interaction<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span></div><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-top:.4cqw'>needs Graph layout and spatial organization</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>A graph interface must support selecting, inspecting, creating, editing, and connecting entities. Panning, zooming, focus, search, and progressive disclosure help users navigate large structures without losing context.</div></div></div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#94a3b8'>5</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Semantic zoom<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span></div><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-top:.4cqw'>needs Navigation and interaction</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>Semantic zoom changes the representation of information as the viewing scale changes. A node might appear as an icon when distant, a summary when closer, and a complete interactive document when examined in detail. This differs from simply enlarging the same picture.</div><div style='margin-top:.8cqw;font:400 1.6cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155'><span style='color:#4d7c0f;font:800 1.2cqw/1 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase'>article</span> <b style='font-weight:700;color:#1f2937'>Graph visualization and interaction research</b> · Search visualization research literature for graph drawing, information visualization, and semantic zoom.</div></div></div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#94a3b8'>6</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Typed relationships and schemas<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span></div><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-top:.4cqw'>needs Nodes, edges, and properties</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>Nodes and edges can have defined types, properties, and constraints. Typed relationships allow software to distinguish containment, dependency, causation, sequence, and other meanings instead of treating every connection as an arbitrary line.</div></div></div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#94a3b8'>7</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Views and projections<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span></div><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-top:.4cqw'>needs Typed relationships and schemas</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>The same underlying information can produce multiple interfaces: diagrams, documents, cards, tables, timelines, and interactive controls. A projection presents the graph for a particular purpose without requiring a separate authoritative copy of its information.</div></div></div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#94a3b8'>8</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>Persistence and addressability<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span></div><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-top:.4cqw'>needs Typed relationships and schemas</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>A useful graph interface needs stable identities, reliable storage, and ways to reference information across contexts. Addressable graphs can support sharing, reuse, composition, and collaboration while preserving the underlying information independently of its presentation.</div></div></div><div style='display:flex;gap:2.4cqw;margin-bottom:2.4cqw'><div style='flex:0 0 5cqw;font:800 2.4cqw/1.2 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#94a3b8'>9</div><div style='min-width:0;flex:1;padding:1.6cqw 2cqw;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0'><div style='font:700 2.1cqw/1.3 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#1f2937'>AI and graph-native authoring<span style='display:inline-block;margin-left:1.2cqw;padding:.2cqw 1.2cqw;border-radius:9cqw;font:700 1.2cqw/1.4 Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;background:#fff;color:#94a3b8;border:1px solid #94a3b8'>Not yet</span></div><div style='font:italic 1.5cqw/1.5 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#64748b;margin-top:.4cqw'>needs Views and projections, Persistence and addressability</div><div style='font:400 1.7cqw/1.55 Georgia,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,serif;color:#334155;margin-top:.4cqw'>AI can interact with graphs as structured information rather than interpreting screenshots or manipulating opaque interfaces. Given a clear schema and mutation contract, an AI can create entities, connect concepts, modify existing structures, and collaborate with human authors while preserving durable state.</div></div></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "The Detail view: the page in full. The Method writes it from the masthead, the section and the routes, so edit those and not this.",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
