      "data": {
        "title": "Graphs versus hierarchies",
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/learn-a-topic/concept.node-class.node",
        "body": "Traditional interfaces commonly organize information into trees: folders, menus, and nested documents. Graphs permit multiple relationships between the same entities and allow information to participate in several contexts without duplicating it.",
